  "tol": 0.01,
  "options": [],
  "explain": "<p><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mn>7</mn><mo>≈</mo><mn>0.43</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(p - 1)/(m + p - 1) = 3/7 \\approx 0.43</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">p</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">m</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7778em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">p</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">3/7</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≈</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.43</span></span></span></span>: almost half the time idle. With 32 micro-batches it falls to <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mn>35</mn><mo>≈</mo><mn>0.09</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">3/35 \\approx 0.09</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">3/35</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≈</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.09</span></span></span></span>, which is why pipelines need many micro-batches per step, and why the global batch limits how deep a pipeline can usefully be.</p>"
 },
 {
  "id": "L18/p4",
  "lesson": "L18",
  "kind": "prediction",
  "prompt": "<p>On one of 8 GPUs the loss comes out NaN, and the training loop's guard <code>if loss.isnan(): continue</code> skips that step on that GPU only. What happens?</p>",
  "answer": "d",
  "answerKind": "choice",
  "tol": 0,
  "options": [
   {
    "key": "a",
    "html": "<p>That GPU's update is skipped and training continues normally.</p>"
   },
   {
    "key": "b",
    "html": "<p>The other GPUs average 7 gradients instead of 8.</p>"
   },
   {
    "key": "c",
    "html": "<p>An exception is raised on every GPU.</p>"
   },
   {
    "key": "d",
    "html": "<p>The other seven GPUs wait forever in their all-reduce, and the job hangs.</p>"
   }
  ],
  "explain": "<p>A collective completes only when every rank calls it. The rank that skipped moves on to the next step's forward pass while the other seven block in the gradient all-reduce, and from then on the ranks issue their collectives out of step. Nothing crashes; the job just stops making progress until a timeout kills it. Decisions that change which collectives run must be made together, with a collective of their own.</p>"
 },
 {
  "id": "L18/concept1",
  "lesson": "L18",
  "kind": "concept",
  "prompt": "How many bytes per parameter does mixed-precision Adam training need for model states?",
  "answer": "About 16: 2 for 16-bit weights, 2 for 16-bit gradients, and 12 for fp32 master weights, momentum and variance.",
  "answerKind": "text"
 },
 {
  "id": "L18/concept2",
  "lesson": "L18",
  "kind": "concept",
  "prompt": "What does each GPU send in a ring all-reduce of n bytes over P GPUs?",
  "answer": "2 (P - 1) / P times n bytes: a reduce-scatter and an all-gather, each moving (P - 1) / P of the data, almost independent of P.",
  "answerKind": "text"
 },
 {
  "id": "L18/concept3",
  "lesson": "L18",
  "kind": "concept",
  "prompt": "What do ZeRO stages 1, 2 and 3 shard?",
  "answer": "Stage 1 the optimizer states, stage 2 also the gradients, stage 3 also the weights, each over the data-parallel ranks.",
  "answerKind": "text"
 },
 {
  "id": "L18/concept4",
  "lesson": "L18",
  "kind": "concept",
  "prompt": "How does Megatron-style tensor parallelism split an MLP?",
  "answer": "The first layer by columns and the second by rows, so each GPU computes a slice of the hidden units and a partial output, and one all-reduce sums the outputs.",
  "answerKind": "text"
 },
 {
  "id": "L18/concept5",
  "lesson": "L18",
  "kind": "concept",
  "prompt": "What is the pipeline bubble?",
  "answer": "The idle fraction (p - 1) / (m + p - 1) of a pipeline with p stages and m micro-batches, while the pipeline fills and drains.",
  "answerKind": "text"
 },
 {
  "id": "L18/concept6",
  "lesson": "L18",
  "kind": "concept",
  "prompt": "What does activation checkpointing trade?",
  "answer": "Memory for compute: it keeps only some activations and recomputes the rest during backward, at the cost of about one extra forward pass.",
  "answerKind": "text"
 },
